      "belief": {
       "@type": "belief",
       "@id": "copies/sj582bt2976.jsonld#date-belief",
       "certainty": "possible",
       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/sj582bt2976.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "A stamp, not a hand, set across the roll in w1 and well clear of the crop edge. Five marks and a point: a heavy leading mark shaped like a serif 1 but carrying a smear of ink at its foot, then 9, 8, an over-inked figure with a counter above a solid base which I take for 2, and 5. Read straight through this is 19. 8. 25. The warning about the stamped rolls applies here: the figures without the leading mark, 9825, already make a possible date, 9. 8. 25., so the day is either 9 or 19 and I cannot choose between them from this impression alone. August 1925 is firm; the fourth figure would have to be a 0 for 1905, and it is not an even ring. w2-w4 show a torn edge, tissue and perforations, with no second impression of the same stamp to compare the leading mark against."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
